    "created_at": "2016-04-29T20:08:42Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-29T20:08:42Z",
    "body": "I don't think I care very much, but `a.js` makes more intuitive sense to me. And it matches the way other parts of the spec work: `HostResolveImportedModule` sees `a.js` as the referencing module for `b.js`, and URL resolution is (of course) relative to `a.js`.\n",
